<article class="page-body">
<header class="page-header"><h1>Privacy</h1></header>
<p>This site is a static blog. It has no accounts, comments, or forms.</p>
<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count page views and see which pages people read. The data goes to Google LLC, which may process it in the United States. It includes the pages you visit, the site that referred you, your browser and device type, and your approximate location (country or city, derived from your IP address). I see this only as aggregated reports and use it only to decide what to write and fix on this site. I do not use it for advertising.</p>
<p>Google Analytics sets first-party cookies named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, which expire after up to two years. If you visit from the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, these cookies are not set: the site tells Google Analytics not to store anything on your device, and Google receives only cookieless page-view signals.</p>
<p>Google processes this data under its own terms: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. You can block it with your browser's cookie settings, a content blocker, or the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p>
<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes basic request data (such as IP address) to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse.</p>
<h2>Email</h2>
<p>If you email me, I use your address and message only to reply. I do not add you to a mailing list or share your email.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
